BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 1 of 4) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: Silberschatz - OS Concepts \(Ch. 8 - 10th Edition Revised\)) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (Chapter 8: Deadlocks \(10th Edition Revised\)) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (8.1 System Model & Modern Multicore Architectures) Tj T* (In revised multicore architectures, resources are categorized with hardware affinity.) Tj T* (A process must request a resource before using it and must release it afterwards.) Tj T* (Deadlock occurs when every thread in a set is blocked waiting for an event that only another) Tj T* (blocked thread in the same set can trigger.) Tj T* ET
