4 0 obj
<< /Length 905 >>
stream
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 2 of 4) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: Silberschatz - OS Concepts \(Ch. 8 - 10th Edition Revised\)) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (8.2 Deadlock Characterization: Updated Coffman Criteria) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (The 10th edition refines the classical 1971 Coffman definition for modern distributed locks:) Tj T* (1. Mutual Exclusion: At least one resource must be held in an exclusive lock mode.) Tj T* (2. Hold and Wait: A process holds at least one resource and requests additional locks.) Tj T* (3. No Preemption: Resources cannot be preempted; lock release is cooperative only.) Tj T* (   *Revision note: Non-cooperative thread termination now introduces orphan mutex issues.*) Tj T* (4. Circular Wait: A closed directed cycle of lock dependencies exists across executing threads.) Tj T* ET
endstream
