BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 3 of 4) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: Silberschatz - OS Concepts \(Ch. 8 - 10th Edition Revised\)) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (8.3 Clarified Starvation Metrics & Benchmarks) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* /F2 10 Tf (    "Revised Definition: Deadlock is a static terminal state with 0% throughput across the blocked set.") Tj /F1 11 Tf T* /F2 10 Tf (    "Starvation is a dynamic performance pathology where system throughput continues normally while specific threads suffer infinite latency.") Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (Statistical benchmarks show starvation occurs 14x more frequently than deadlock in cloud clusters) Tj T* (due to non-uniform priority queuing and tail-latency scheduling anomalies.) Tj T* ET
endstream
